{"text":"Repair the workroom list sorting, filtered counts, and tab-switch correctness on a fresh request/ui-list-correctness branch. Deliver the reviewed exact head to main, push origin/main, and remove the merged worktree and branch.","body":{"conditions":"1. Initial sorting from either Age or # is recent first: the youngest age or greatest ticket number appears first. Preserve a clear reversible header sort cycle and the existing priority default when no explicit column sort is active.\n2. While the search box filters rows, every tab count is computed from that same search-filtered population before the selected tab is applied. Clearing search restores the unfiltered counts.\n3. Switching tabs replaces the rendered table population exactly. Reproduce Completed to Open and repeated back-and-forth switching: no completed-only row appears under Open, no row is duplicated, and every repetition remains idempotent. The rendered unique row keys and row count must match the selected filtered population after each switch.\n4. Add deterministic regression tests for recent-first Age and #, filtered per-tab counts, and repeated tab switching. Include a test that fails against the current leaking and duplicating behavior.\n5. Keep unrelated row semantics, selected-thread behavior, keyboard/accessibility behavior, and the current architecture contract unchanged unless the implementation genuinely changes that contract; update docs/reference/architecture.md in the same head if it does.\n6. Run the proportional UI, embed-parity, Go, formatting, and mutation-sensitive gates; publish exact changed-path artifacts; obtain independent Architecture, Security, and Simplification review; ratify approval; merge only that approved exact head; push main; then delete the merged worktree and branch. This is a delivery request. No report may satisfy it before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec